<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">resurrect</ansi>

A companion who dies isn't gone at once. They stay on your roster, dead,
keeping whatever gear their body kept, and you have <ansi fg="yellow">3 game days</ansi> to have
them raised. Only the time you're logged in counts, and you're warned
when half an hour is left.

A church (in a city) or a village shaman can raise them, if the keeper is
there. Coming back costs the companion one level (never below 1). If time
runs out, the companion is lost for good.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">resurrect</ansi>
  List your dead companions and how long each has left.

  <ansi fg="command">resurrect [member]</ansi>
  Have a companion raised, at a church or shaman.

<ansi fg="command">company status</ansi> also lists the dead and the lost. See <ansi fg="command">help death</ansi> for
your own death.
